 {n:"Workflows defined in the console",s:["An administrator can define a multi-step workflow from the console as stored, versioned data, and an agent assigned that workflow runs it without a person performing each step","A workflow step can call a skill, read a connector or use a tool, and every such step runs through the gate at the run's reach, the leash and the meter, exactly as an agent's own call does","A workflow step's output is named and schema-checked, and a later step can read only outputs that earlier steps declared","A workflow step can run only when a condition over earlier named outputs holds, and a skipped step is recorded as skipped with the condition that decided it","Workflow steps declared parallel start together, and the step that combines them runs only after each has finished or been recorded as a gap","Each workflow step carries its own retry limit and backoff, a side-effecting step is retried only through its idempotency key, and a step that exhausts its retries takes its declared failure path","Every finished workflow or automation run emits a success or failure signal naming the workflow, the agent and the step that failed, and repeated failures of one step open a learning candidate instead of changing the workflow","A workflow that reads two connectors, calls two skills, waits for an approval and delivers a document runs end to end on the install and leaves one trace a person can follow"]},
 {n:"Found by tracing every requirement to a task",s:["The monthly search report workflow runs on the install for a named client: it resolves the client, reads the period's analytics and search console figures, finds the previous report, runs the search checks, writes recommendations into the report template, holds it for approval and delivers it, and no step but the approval is performed by a person, with the run recorded","A scheduler inside the application runs every registered scheduled control when it is due, holding a database lock so two application copies never run the same one, and a control with no run inside its window raises an alert","Automations are proved on an install: a scheduled, a connector-event and a webhook automation each run as their owner from a named template, one is suspended when its owner loses a required access and offered for adoption when the owner leaves, run history shows cost and outcome, and where the optional canvas is enabled it reaches the platform only over the internal network, with the checks recorded","Workflow control flow is proved on an install: a workflow with two parallel skill steps, a conditional step that is skipped, a step that fails, retries through its idempotency key and takes its failure path, and a combining step that records the gap shows every outcome in its one trace, with the checks recorded","The automation gallery ships a daily brief, capture of deals from group chats into the customer records held as drafts, and drafted email replies a person sends, each declaring its trigger, connectors and approval step","Every notice the product composes is delivered to the person it names through their bound channel or the configured email relay, and a notice that could not be delivered is shown as undelivered on the notifications screen","An agent runs only the workflows assigned to it, and a request that would start any other workflow through it is refused before the first step runs","Every human approval requirement in the requirements register is demonstrated on an install by a person, and each check is recorded against the requirement it proves","On the install the denial digest runs on its window and tells the person's department lead or data steward that someone keeps being refused, naming no resource they could not reach"]}
